# ============================================================
# Modelfile for qwen3.8:27b-nvfp4 (Qwen3.8-27B, dense)
# M5 Pro, 48GB unified memory — second-opinion / hard problems
# Pull first: ollama pull qwen3.8:27b-nvfp4   (~18GB download)
# Build: ollama create qwen3.8-thinker -f Modelfile.qwen3.8-27b
# ============================================================

# Qwen3.8-27B — dense 27B, 262K native context, multimodal
# (image input), released 2026-08-14. On paper the strongest
# local coder in its class (SWE-bench Pro 61.7, LiveCodeBench
# v6 90.3), but dense means every token reads all ~18GB of
# weights: expect 15-30 tok/s on the M5 Pro's 307GB/s
# bandwidth. Use it for deliberate hand-offs (design review,
# gnarly bugs, screenshot analysis), not the inner agent loop —
# that's qwen3.6-coder's job.
#
# nvfp4 is Ollama's 4-bit format for the Apple MLX path:
# ~20% faster generation than q4_K_M at roughly half the
# quantization quality loss.
FROM qwen3.8:27b-nvfp4

# ── Sampling parameters ─────────────────────────────────────

# Qwen's published preset for 3.8 thinking mode: temperature
# 1.0, top_p 0.95, top_k 20, presence_penalty 0.0. (The
# instruct/non-thinking preset differs — temp 0.7, top_p 0.8,
# presence 1.5 — switch to those if running with thinking
# disabled, or the model may loop.)
PARAMETER temperature 1.0
PARAMETER top_p 0.95
PARAMETER top_k 20
PARAMETER min_p 0.0
PARAMETER presence_penalty 0.0
PARAMETER repeat_penalty 1.0

# ── Reasoning effort ────────────────────────────────────────

# The model defaults to reasoning_effort=xhigh, which burns
# tens of thousands of thinking tokens per turn — measured 21
# minutes for one answer on consumer hardware. ALWAYS run at
# low: reports have it behaving like a frontier model on high
# even at low effort. Ollama can't pin this in a Modelfile —
# set it per session (`ollama run qwen3.8-thinker --think=low`,
# verify the flag is honored by watching whether responses
# start within seconds) or per request via the API's `think`
# field / your harness's reasoning-effort setting.

# ── Context window ──────────────────────────────────────────

# Dense-attention KV cache is much larger per token than
# qwen3.6-coder's hybrid layout, and this model's role is
# focused hand-offs, not repo-wide agent sessions — 64K is
# plenty and keeps total load ~24GB, inside the default Metal
# wired limit. Same caveat as always: a client-sent num_ctx
# silently overrides this. Verify with `ollama ps`.
PARAMETER num_ctx 65536
